    "module_designation": null,
    "description": "Electromagnetic water meters type BFG070 designed to measure, memorise and display the volume at metering conditions of water passing through the measurement transducer. They consist of a flow sensor and an electronic calculating/indicating device. The flow sensor measures based on an induction principle with hard rubber lining, straight inlet (5 times the diameter) and outlet (3 times the diameter) length, without flow conditioner; the meter is designed to measure reverse flow. The meter must be equipped with a plastic cover over the electronics with a conductive coating on the inside; the LCD display is protected by a conductive metallic foil and all components must be conductively connected. Equipped with electronic indicating device (LCD) showing delivered volumes in cubic meters (positive, negative, total); normal resolution mode displays up to 00000000.001 m³/h and 00000000.001 m³, high resolution mode (used during calibration, set by factory tool protected by user, service and factory passwords) shows volume resolution of 0.001 L. Software version is shown after reset; checksum displayed via Info – FW Checksum. To be installed with the flow axis in horizontal and vertical (bottom-to-top and top-to-bottom) planes. Securing: one of the screws connecting the meter body and counter case is connected with the butts on the electronic output by a wire with a seal."
